    "result_text": "A steward can now reopen a closed period, and the acceptance test passes when run with `bin/e2e`.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Who can reopen:** only a steward. If anyone else tries, or the period isn't closed, the server refuses with a 400. Nothing is saved and nothing is written to the audit file.\n- **What reopening does:** it marks the period open and drops the total that was saved when it was closed. The due-total is then worked out live again. In the test it went from the saved `1.00` to `2.00` under the new rate.\n- **Audit:** a successful reopen writes `PERIOD_REOPENED sheet=<id> by=<user> period=<name>`.\n- **Screen:** each period row has a new Reopen button (`period-reopen`). A refusal shows in the row's existing `period-error`. If the period isn't closed, the screen shows the error itself without calling the server, the same way Close already does.\n\n**Files:**\n- New endpoint `periods/{name}/reopen.POST.yml`, with two new classes: `ReopenPeriod` (the steward and closed checks) and `AuditPeriodReopened` (the audit line).\n- A `reopen()` method in `Period.java`.\n- The button and the call behind it in `periods.slot.tsx` and `periods.ts`.\n\nNo database change was needed, because the existing `closed` and `closed_total` columns cover a reopened period.",
